/ Fix, then go on from the same step: Work's first step throws while 'workspace/broken.txt' exists. Its handler fixes the
/ cause (deletes the file), then starts the error's callback, which goes on from the step that threw, in an app of its
/ own: the step runs again, no longer throws, and that run goes on to its end, through this goal too, answering
/ "completed". The callback is the run as it stood at the throw, so %resumed% is set only here, in the asker.
Start
- write "broken" to file 'workspace/broken.txt'
- call Work
- if %resumed% is not empty
    - assert %resumed% equals "completed", "the callback's run should have gone on to its end"
- return "completed"

/ The step that throws while the file exists, its handler the fix.
Work
- if file 'workspace/broken.txt' exists
    - throw error "boom", on error call CaptureCallback

/ The fix, then the run goes on from the step that threw.
CaptureCallback
- delete file 'workspace/broken.txt'
- set %cb% = %!error.callback%
- callback.start callback=%cb%, write to %resumed%
